{"seq":13,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T17:02:19.705Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a1049ae35796d6e685749ec50d12b9ad8ebb92c8f8bea1292656ccd5142fda71","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes that you can read:\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments not reaching drivers at Doors 14–18. Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025, and support confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md` (\"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\"), under \"What Changed\" and \"Action Items\".\n- **#4419**: Gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Thea logged it, and the cheat sheet says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md` (\"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\"), under \"Account & Operational Notes\" and \"What Changed\".\n\nTwo other digests mention QFL but have no ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in.\n\nI left out the Central handoffs digest (#4409 and #4412). Those belong to Pree's dealer account, not QFL. I also left out the 2025 handoff email that mentions #4419, since it isn't one of Moss's notes.\n\nYour April 2026 debrief note also has #8841, but that's your own note, not Moss's, so I haven't counted it here."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
